   "text": "Identifying Red & White Blood Cells"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- You need to be able to identify red and white blood cells in photomicrographs and diagrams\n\n  - Red blood cells have a concave disc shape with no nucleus\n  - White blood cells are usually round in shape with a nucleus"
  },
