  {
   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_gsjnWZwqkPN53VFF",
   "name": "Components of Blood: Function",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Components of Blood: Function"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Plasma is important for the **transport** of carbon dioxide, digested food (nutrients), urea, mineral ions, hormones and heat energy\n- Red blood cells **transport oxygen** around the body from the lungs to cells which require it for aerobic respiration\n\n  - They carry the oxygen in the form of oxyhaemoglobin\n- White blood cells **defend** the body against infection by pathogens by carrying out **phagocytosis** and **antibody production**\n- Platelets are involved in helping the **blood to clot**"
  }
